# Target C: eliminate the two-rank-two singleton branch of Profile B

Date: 2026-09-23

Status: rigorous closure of the remaining Profile B subcase with two rank-two local-empty singleton blocks. Combined with the previously proved global upper bound of two, every genuine remaining eight-no-root `k=6,D=-1,p=9` Profile B source has at most one rank-two singleton block and therefore at least eight aligned singleton blocks. This does not close Profile B or Target C-II.

Companion exact certificate:

`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k6_dminus1_profile_b_two_ranktwo_touch3_closure_2026_09_23.py`

The inputs are already proved in the repository:

```text
rank(P)=2,
d_1(P)>=4,
exactly nine singleton changed blocks,
at most two rank-two local-empty singleton blocks,
```

and every genuine remaining Profile B source has a dependency-active aligned singleton block `b` touched by exactly three source cycles. If `T` is that three-coordinate touch set, then deleting `T` gives the distinguished rank-preserving `d_5=2` puncture from the touch-three kernel witness.

Assume for contradiction that there are two rank-two singleton blocks `c,d`. Let their nonzero coefficient lines be `L_c,L_d <= P`. They are distinct and span `P`.

## 1. The forced touch-three set contains a coefficient-zero column

The three selected cycles in `T` lie in one aligned local direction star of `b`.

The previously proved line-star intersection bound says that the support of a rank-two singleton coefficient line meets any distinct aligned star in at most one source coordinate. Hence

```text
|supp(L_c) intersect T| <= 1,
|supp(L_d) intersect T| <= 1.
```

Each line is therefore zero on at least two of the three coordinates of `T`. Two subsets of a three-set, each of size at least two, intersect. Thus some coordinate of `T` is zero for both independent lines `L_c,L_d`. Since those lines span the rank-two plane `P`, that coordinate is a zero column of `P`.

Consequently

```text
d_2(P) <= 7.                                      (1.1)
```

The singleton-line sharpening already proves that `d_2(P)=5` permits at most one rank-two singleton block. Since two are assumed, only

```text
d_2(P) in {6,7}                                  (1.2)
```

remains. This removes `d_2(P)=8` without computation.

## 2. The `d_2(P)=7` branch reduces to one common-two-set census

Suppose `d_2(P)=7`. There is exactly one coefficient-zero column, and by Section 1 it lies in `T`.

The two rank-two coefficient lines cannot use the same nonzero coordinate of `T`: otherwise the other two coordinates of `T` would both be zero for both lines, giving two zero columns. Thus, after ordering the lines, the three positions of `T` have support signatures

```text
c-only, d-only, zero.                              (2.1)
```

Let `m_c,m_d` be the multiplicities of the two projective column classes killed by `L_c,L_d`. The sharpened projective-column inequality gives

```text
m_c,m_d <= 3,
m_c+m_d >= 5.
```

Thus, up to ordering,

```text
(m_c,m_d) in {(3,3),(2,3),(3,2)}.
```

Their support intersection has size

```text
7-m_c-m_d in {1,2},
```

so it is nonempty. Therefore the root triples of `c,d` share two vertices. The `c`-only and `d`-only coordinates in `T` show that each of `c,d` also shares two root vertices with `b`. Hence `b,c,d` are three distinct pairwise two-intersecting triples.

As in the preceding touch-four closure, the tetrahedral-face type is impossible. In that type all three root pairs use one four-set, while one aligned star of `b` contains only one orientation on that four-set; (2.1) requires two distinct star coordinates, one meeting `c` and one meeting `d`.

The only incidence type is therefore the common-two-set type. Up to `S_7`, normalize

```text
b=123,
c=124,
d=125.
```

The outside-vertex permutation normalizes the three selected star members and omitted fourth member as

```text
fourth 4: c-only,
fourth 5: d-only,
fourth 6: zero,
fourth 7: omitted.
```

The certificate enumerates all three local directions at each of `b,c,d`, all three projective multiplicity possibilities above, and every five-cycle completion outside the `b`-star consistent with the resulting support counts. It then checks exactly over `Q`:

1. `rank(P)=2`;
2. `d_2(P)=7` and `d_1(P)>=4`;
3. local empty ranks `1,2,2` at `b,c,d`;
4. the chosen aligned/rank-two singleton constraints are contained in `P` while the empty spaces are not;
5. the exact virtual-canonical source deficiency `d_8`.

Exactly

```text
1188
```

normalized coefficient/source states survive these necessary local conditions, with deficiency histogram

```text
d_8=6: 384
d_8=7: 608
d_8=8: 196.
```

There is no `d_8=3` state. Hence `d_2(P)=7` is impossible in the two-rank-two branch.

## 3. Structure when `d_2(P)=6`

Now suppose `d_2(P)=6`. There are exactly two coefficient-zero columns.

The minimum-distance bound gives projective multiplicity at most two, while the pairwise singleton-line inequality gives

```text
m_c+m_d >= 4.
```

Hence

```text
m_c=m_d=2,
wt(L_c)=wt(L_d)=4,
|supp(L_c) intersect supp(L_d)|=2.                (3.1)
```

There are two cases according to how many of the two global zero columns lie in `T`.

### 3.1 Exactly one zero column lies in `T`

Then the same argument as in Section 2 forces the signatures on `T` to be

```text
c-only, d-only, zero.
```

The support intersection in (3.1) is nonempty, so again `b,c,d` are pairwise two-intersecting and the tetrahedral type is impossible. Normalize the same common-two-set geometry `123,124,125`.

Outside `T`, (3.1) forces exactly

```text
2 both,
1 c-only,
1 d-only,
1 zero
```

among the five selected cycles avoiding `b`.

The exact normalized census contains

```text
5312
```

states satisfying the local rank, coefficient-distance, and virtual-completeness conditions. Their deficiency histogram is

```text
d_8=6:  192
d_8=7: 4448
d_8=8:  480
d_8=9:  144
d_8=10:  48.
```

Again there is no `d_8=3` state.

### 3.2 Both zero columns lie in `T`

The third coordinate of `T` is nonzero. It is either in both coefficient-line supports or in exactly one of them.

If it lies in both supports, then `b,c,d` are three faces of its four-set. Every no-root cycle touching both `c,d` then lies on that same four-set and therefore also touches `b`. But (3.1) requires two common-support coordinates, while only one lies in `T` and every other selected source cycle avoids `b`. Contradiction. The certificate independently checks this as zero available outside-`b` `both` cycles for every normalized local-direction pattern.

It remains, up to swapping `c,d`, that the unique nonzero coordinate of `T` is `c`-only. Normalize the omitted star member to fourth vertex 7 and the nonzero member to fourth vertex 4. The certificate deliberately does not normalize the remaining root geometry further: it enumerates every possible `c` face of that four-set and every root block `d` sharing two vertices with `c`, together with all local singleton directions.

Outside `T`, equation (3.1) forces

```text
2 both,
1 c-only,
2 d-only,
0 zero.
```

The exact census contains

```text
7200
```

states satisfying all necessary local conditions. Their deficiency histogram is

```text
d_8=6: 1536
d_8=7: 5664.
```

There is no `d_8=3` state. The `d`-only version is the same census after interchanging the two rank-two lines.

Thus `d_2(P)=6` is also impossible in the two-rank-two branch.

## 4. Consequence

Sections 1--3 exclude every possible coefficient support size for a genuine source with two rank-two singleton blocks. Therefore

```text
number of rank-two local-empty singleton blocks <= 1.     (4.1)
```

Since Profile B has exactly nine singleton changed blocks,

```text
number of aligned singleton blocks >= 8.                  (4.2)
```

The nine source replacement classes form a basis of the nine-dimensional source quotient and `L=W^perp` has dimension six. Hence at least three source classes are dependency-active. At most one of those active classes can belong to a rank-two singleton block, so at least two dependency-active singleton blocks are aligned.

Every dependency-active aligned block has source touch count three or four. The preceding touch-four-alternative closure already proves that at least one has touch count three. Therefore every remaining Profile B source now has one of the sharper forms:

1. at least two dependency-active aligned touch-three blocks, giving at least two distinct distinguished `d_5=2` deletion triples and two coordinate-split kernels `K_T=E_T direct-sum <q_j>`; or
2. one dependency-active aligned touch-three block and at least one additional dependency-active aligned touch-four block.

This is the next source-level split to attack. Profile B and Target C-II remain open.

## 5. Computational status

The counts above were independently reproduced with exact rational arithmetic from the committed K8 four-cycle normal form: the 105 no-root cycles, the 35 root blocks, local quotient components `QCOMP`, singleton determinant rows, virtual-canonical complete-set rule, and complete-block deficiency rank. No finite-field rank decision, random sampling, GitHub Actions, or external runner result is used.

The companion verifier encodes the same normalized finite cases so that the calculation is auditable from the repository.
